{
  "description": "Stricter-only (QA-2): a lower layer may only narrow, for every row of policy-dimensions.json in every layer that may set it, through the one resolver in Node (domain/policy) and Python (harness_core.policy). `ladders` hold one ceiling row each: `top` set by the first layer the row is exposed to, `narrow` a narrower value a lower layer may set (`kept` is the effective value when it differs from `narrow`), `widen` a value wider than `narrow` (refused naming `at`, the row's path unless a member is named; a `meet` row keeps `kept` instead); `base` are layers every case of the row starts from, `hostOnly` rows have no key in an engine profile narrowing. `choices` hold one choice row each (`other` is a second value inside `ceiling`, which a lock refuses below it, C4.02); `operatorSample` is a value for any operator row, which no layer below the deployment may set. `release` is the profile the engine-profile resolver narrows on the `engineProfile.*` ladders, whose `top` values are its own. `efforts` are the requested efforts (run spec) against the profile's reasoningEffort ceiling: `narrowing` is what the request layer asks, `pinned` the profile's effort. `cases` are resolved like policy-resolve.json's. Ladders, choices, efforts and case layers are written by hand; each kept case's config and digest were computed by the Python resolver and reviewed.",
